PLR 3.3.2 stateful data descriptor, FORWARD-REFERENCE order: the
descriptor class (Pos) is defined before the field-owning class (C). The
1a-bis re-pass (third condition: a method accesses an unannotated non-self
param's attribute) re-converts Pos's __get__/__set__ after C's struct (with
its dynamic `_v` field) is registered, so `obj._v` resolves instead of
baking to nondet. Previously KNOWNBUG.
